WEBVTT

00:16:29.726 --> 00:16:34.340
this is the official dogma,
the one that we all take to be true,

00:16:34.364 --> 00:16:36.329
and it's all false.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:37.919
It is not true.

00:16:38.292 --> 00:16:41.971
There's no question that some choice
is better than none.

00:16:42.567 --> 00:16:44.614
But it doesn't follow from that

00:16:44.638 --> 00:16:47.085
that more choice
is better than some choice.

00:16:47.109 --> 00:16:49.647
There's some magical amount.
I don't know what it is.

00:16:49.671 --> 00:16:52.698
I'm pretty confident that we have
long since passed the point

00:16:52.722 --> 00:16:55.087
where options improve our welfare.

00:16:55.452 --> 00:16:58.409
Now, as a policy matter --
I'm almost done --

00:16:58.433 --> 00:17:01.817
as a policy matter,
the thing to think about is this: